/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-03T18:15:03Z","updated_at":"2025-07-03T18:15:03Z","body":"> I wonder if this is a problem really worth solving though. We haven't had reports so far of users being confused by the apparent mismatch between our human-readable names in the editor and the Android permission names in `AndroidManifest.xml`.\n> \n> I get @m4gr3d's point that this would be technically more correct, but is it really solving a problem? Godot users are familiar with the fact that properties names (usually `snake_case`) get converted to \"Title Case\" in the editor by default - they can now even be localized. I don't see how priori how those are particularly different from other properties to warrant a dedicated core change to support them.\n\nIt's not a concern as users are used to the current mechanism, but I'm planning to revamp the way we display the permissions in a future release (currently take too much vertical space) and this new hint would be needed for that refactor.\n\nBut the changes being this small, I can replicate them whenever I update the Android permissions options, so I'm okay with closing this PR for now.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3033146088/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"e